    "lawCode": "Amd §4310, Pub Health L; amd §11-0713, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7318\n\nSPONSOR: KENNEDY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law and the environmental conservation\nlaw, in relation to allowing donate life registration when applying for\nor renewing a hunting, fishing or trapping license\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAllows donate life registration when applying for or renewing a hunting,\nfishing or trapping license in person or electronically.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 5 of Section 4310 of the\nPublic Health Law, to allow registration of organ donor upon applying or\nrenewing a hunting, fishing, or trapping license.\n\nSection 2 amends section 11-0713 of the environmental conservation law,\nby requiring the Commissioner of Department of Environmental Conserva-\ntion (DEC) provide a space on the application in person or electron-\nically to register in the donate life registry.\n\nSection 3 sets effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, the only ways to enroll in the registry are through the\nDepartment of Health, the Department of Motor Vehicles, and the Board of\nElections. Today, nearly 10,000 New Yorkers are waiting for life-saving\norgan transplants, this bill creates another path to increase enrollment\nin the NY Donate Life Registry. Only 22% of eligible New Yorkers (age 18\nand older) are enrolled on the New York State Donate Life Registry\ncompared to the national state average of 47%, as New York is ranked\n49th in registered organ donors. The overall aim is increasing access\nand opportunities to save lives.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS.4471A of 2018 S.6963 of 2017\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect one year after it shall become a law.\n",
